# ::tok A: On February 3, the U.S. Department of Labor released non-farm payrolls data for January 2023, adding 517,000 non-farm payrolls, significantly higher than market expectations of 189,000; the unemployment rate fell to 3.4%, the lowest in nearly 50 years; and hourly wages grew by 4.4% year-on-year and 0.3% month-on-month, slowing slightly.
